    <GaugingStation location="Currypool Farm" name="Currypool Stream" number="52016">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump profile weir opened in 1971 with velocity area station for higher flows in a predominantly Old Red Sandstone and Marl catchment. Weir converted into a 2 crested stainless steel compound Crump weir in winter 2022/2023 to improve the sensitivity and accuracy of the lowest flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Vegetated banks. Likely to go out of bank below bankfull at station. River bed silty and stony. Flood diversion channel just downstream of weir on left-hand bank - excess water channelled across field to prevent flooding downstream. Accretion of silt on right-hand side of weir. Highest flows exceed bankfull, gaugings needed to confirm rating in this range. Two ratings applied across period of record for the original structure. Rating is acceptable to 0.4m, there have been no higher flow gaugings since the last review to be able to confirm the rating beyond low flows. The rating for the new 2 crested compound Crump weir structure is currently proven to a stage of 0.3 metres.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Station opened in 1971. Crump profile weir, crest 4m broad. Velocity area station for flows &gt;1.654 cumecs. Flat pasture on both sides of the river. The original weir was converted into a 2 crested stainless steel compound Crump weir in winter 2022/2023.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Runoff natural to within 10% at Q95. Minor surface water abstraction.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Catchment, predominantly of Old Red Sandstone and Marl, whose headwaters drain the Quantock Hills. Land use is agricultural. No major catchment changes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to within 8% of QMED. Good fit to gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating can not be validated beyond QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
